📗
  ☎️ One connection: reads requests from a transport, runs each through the
  app, and writes the responses, until either side is done.

  Every rule about how HTTP/1.1 messages are framed on a connection lives
  here: where a request ends, when the connection may be reused, and which
  headers describe the body.
